1
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:31,710
What?

2
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:37,960
Stop it.

3
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:39,880
My face is all swollen.

4
00:00:42,030 --> 00:00:43,070
You still look good
even when it's swollen.

5
00:00:43,790 --> 00:00:45,030
But seriously,

6
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:47,920
your wife has terrible taste.

7
00:00:49,110 --> 00:00:50,110
Who cares?

8
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:53,070
Let me help you

9
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:55,430
bring down the swelling.

10
00:01:07,310 --> 00:01:08,120
A ghost.

11
00:01:08,870 --> 00:01:09,680
A ghost!

12
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:11,310
There's a ghost!

13
00:01:27,740 --> 00:01:31,740
=Medical Examiner Dr. Qin: Bones of the Past=
=Episode 18=

14
00:01:34,310 --> 00:01:35,430
This biological sample
is very important.

15
00:01:35,430 --> 00:01:36,040
Please arrange

16
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,280
DNA extraction
and comparison as soon as possible.

17
00:01:40,790 --> 00:01:41,280
Section Chief Qin.

18
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:43,710
This sample appears to be quite old.

19
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:45,710
It's not in ideal condition,

20
00:01:46,590 --> 00:01:48,120
which may affect
the extraction efficiency.

21
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:50,950
Do your best. It's thirty years old.

22
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:52,400
Understood.

23
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:54,710
Since the sample is so important,

24
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:56,040
I'll get the results
as soon as possible.

25
00:01:56,150 --> 00:01:57,150
Qin, there's been a murder.

26
00:01:57,150 --> 00:01:57,840
Come with me to the scene.

27
00:01:57,840 --> 00:01:58,480
Hurry.

28
00:02:00,430 --> 00:02:01,790
The caller's name is Nie Yifeng.

29
00:02:01,790 --> 00:02:03,000
He said someone died in his house.

30
00:02:03,230 --> 00:02:04,710
He said he saw someone with long,
disheveled hair,

31
00:02:04,710 --> 00:02:05,640
wearing a white dress,

32
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:07,280
like a female ghost glaring at him.

33
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:09,560
What century are we in?
There's no such thing as a ghost.

34
00:02:21,590 --> 00:02:22,430
Officer,

35
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:25,000
this is really terrifying.

36
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:26,190
Can you find a way

37
00:02:26,430 --> 00:02:27,840
to get her out of here
as soon as possible?

38
00:02:27,870 --> 00:02:28,680
Otherwise,

39
00:02:28,710 --> 00:02:30,400
how am I supposed to live in this house?

40
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:38,870
Let's go upstairs and take a look.

41
00:03:01,470 --> 00:03:03,360
Jiang, bring the caller over.

42
00:03:03,470 --> 00:03:04,120
Yes.

43
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:15,150
Take a look.

44
00:03:15,910 --> 00:03:17,150
What's your relationship
with the victim?

45
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:19,310
This really has nothing
to do with me, Officer.

46
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:20,520
I didn't get home until late last night.

47
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:21,750
I'm asking you to take a look.

48
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:33,630
Stay there. Don't move.

49
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:35,240
Don't disturb the scene.

50
00:03:41,370 --> 00:03:42,290
Who is the victim?

51
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:47,000
She's my wife.

52
00:03:47,710 --> 00:03:48,910
Yes, yes.

53
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,310
She's my wife, Officer.

54
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:53,680
But...

55
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:55,590
But she left
on a business trip yesterday afternoon.

56
00:03:55,590 --> 00:03:57,080
How could she be here?

57
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:00,560
How is that possible?

58
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:06,520
How is that possible?

59
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:11,910
Chief.

60
00:04:12,310 --> 00:04:14,080
Based on our Economic Crime
Investigation Unit's investigation,

61
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:16,000
the gold you found at the villa

62
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,480
was illicit funds
from the Urban Construction Group.

63
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:18,920
We'll convert the gold
and the seized villa

64
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:20,000
into cash

65
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,310
and return it to the victims.

66
00:04:21,510 --> 00:04:22,800
That's good news.

67
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,190
At least those victims
will get some restitution.

68
00:04:25,270 --> 00:04:26,070
Yes.

69
00:04:26,190 --> 00:04:27,000
Chief.

70
00:04:27,270 --> 00:04:28,870
Wouldn't you say

71
00:04:28,870 --> 00:04:30,920
we've made some progress?

72
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:33,630
Shouldn't you show
some appreciation for those of us

73
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:34,800
on the front lines?

74
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:37,920
Everyone has worked hard lately.

75
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:40,040
We've also made
a major breakthrough in the case.

76
00:04:40,270 --> 00:04:41,870
Now that we've found the crime scene,

77
00:04:41,870 --> 00:04:42,870
we're not far from solving the case.

78
00:04:42,870 --> 00:04:44,560
I'm sure we'll solve it very soon.

79
00:04:44,630 --> 00:04:45,600
- Good.
- Good.

80
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:46,430
Chief.

81
00:04:46,430 --> 00:04:48,510
You can't just show
your appreciation with words.

82
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:50,240
You could at least
treat everyone to a meal.

83
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:51,070
By the way, Qin,

84
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:52,510
it's a good thing you told me in advance

85
00:04:52,510 --> 00:04:53,630
that Zhao Qian had AIDS.

86
00:04:53,830 --> 00:04:55,560
Otherwise, my assistant
and I would've been in serious trouble.

87
00:04:55,750 --> 00:04:56,950
I really have to thank you.

88
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:58,240
I'll pass your thanks

89
00:04:58,310 --> 00:04:59,630
on to our future consultant.

90
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:23,860
(Longfan City People's Hospital,
Outpatient Hall)

91
00:05:28,950 --> 00:05:31,040
Go check on the patient in Bed 7 later.

92
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:32,070
Okay. Don't worry.

93
00:05:45,070 --> 00:05:45,870
Zhuang?

94
00:05:52,830 --> 00:05:53,750
All the dishes are ready.

95
00:05:55,390 --> 00:05:57,360
It's not often our whole family
gets to have a meal together.

96
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,430
Come on. Let's eat.

97
00:05:58,430 --> 00:05:59,190
Wait.

98
00:06:03,040 --> 00:06:03,950
This is for you.

99
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:07,000
Did you get a bonus?

100
00:06:07,310 --> 00:06:08,480
A bonus is nothing.

101
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:09,600
Once the case is solved,

102
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:11,920
there'll be
an even bigger reward waiting for me.

103
00:06:12,430 --> 00:06:14,480
When I grow up,
I want to be a police officer too.

104
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:16,560
I'll buy Mom lipstick too.

105
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:19,270
Our Ming is such a good boy.

106
00:06:19,310 --> 00:06:20,950
But don't become
a police officer like your dad.

107
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,040
It's too dangerous.

108
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:23,870
Join the Navy, okay?

109
00:06:23,870 --> 00:06:24,630
Let's eat.

110
00:06:25,190 --> 00:06:25,720
Let's eat.

111
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:26,680
Time to eat.

112
00:06:30,870 --> 00:06:32,720
I ran into someone I know
at the hospital today.

113
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:34,830
He looked completely distraught.

114
00:06:36,390 --> 00:06:38,830
I didn't expect it to be someone I knew.

115
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:40,190
And then?

116
00:06:43,510 --> 00:06:44,830
Don't you want to ask who it was?

117
00:06:44,830 --> 00:06:45,510
Dad.

118
00:06:46,950 --> 00:06:47,750
Good boy.

119
00:06:48,630 --> 00:06:50,560
It looked like
he was getting tested for AIDS.

120
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:52,950
Who was it?

121
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,270
I don't want to tell you anymore.

122
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:57,720
Egg.

123
00:06:59,310 --> 00:07:00,630
Why are you so annoying?

124
00:07:01,830 --> 00:07:02,870
Fine, I'll tell you.

125
00:07:03,390 --> 00:07:04,430
It was Zhuang.

126
00:07:06,070 --> 00:07:07,240
You scared me.

127
00:07:08,070 --> 00:07:09,360
You know
what things are like for his family.

128
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:10,390
They've had a hard time.

129
00:07:10,830 --> 00:07:12,240
Could it be that after he was burned,

130
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:13,430
he didn't keep the wound clean?

131
00:07:13,870 --> 00:07:14,630
I was thinking

132
00:07:14,630 --> 00:07:15,830
maybe I should check on him.

133
00:07:15,830 --> 00:07:16,680
I'm going out.

134
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:18,920
You're not eating?

135
00:07:20,950 --> 00:07:22,870
Mom, I'm going out too.

136
00:07:23,190 --> 00:07:24,310
You're not eating either?

137
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:28,630
Is my cooking really that bad?

138
00:07:28,660 --> 00:07:29,940
(Attendance)

139
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:40,620
(Attendance Register)

140
00:07:41,340 --> 00:07:44,100
(Attendance Register)

141
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:45,000
Boss,

142
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:46,240
you dragged me here

143
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:47,920
in such a hurry at mealtime

144
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:50,430
just to check
Zhuang Haitao's attendance?

145
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:52,190
He's an honest, hardworking man.

146
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,870
Even when he was injured before,

147
00:07:55,310 --> 00:07:56,800
he still came to work
despite his injury.

148
00:07:57,270 --> 00:07:59,160
Making a living isn't easy for him.

149
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:01,430
Let's not be so hard on him.

150
00:08:02,190 --> 00:08:03,870
He went to the hospital
for an AIDS test.

151
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:05,950
What?

152
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:09,070
AIDS?

153
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:13,120
Zhuang Haitao has AIDS?

154
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:15,310
That can't be.

155
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:17,830
I know Zhuang.

156
00:08:17,870 --> 00:08:19,560
He's just a cleaner.

157
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:22,240
He doesn't sleep around either.

158
00:08:22,270 --> 00:08:23,870
Why would he get tested for AIDS?

159
00:08:24,310 --> 00:08:25,120
Then...

160
00:08:27,190 --> 00:08:28,480
There's only one possibility.

161
00:08:30,190 --> 00:08:31,390
He had contact with Zhao Qian.

162
00:08:33,700 --> 00:08:36,100
(Zhuang Haitao,
half-day leave in the afternoon)

163
00:08:36,550 --> 00:08:37,360
Look here.

164
00:08:39,910 --> 00:08:41,750
On the day of the Body in a Box Case,
he took the afternoon off.

165
00:08:44,270 --> 00:08:46,080
Your wife went on a business trip
and you didn't hear from her.

166
00:08:46,870 --> 00:08:48,200
You never thought to contact her?

167
00:08:49,270 --> 00:08:50,600
She often travels alone for work.

168
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:52,910
We're both used to it.

169
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:55,200
Besides, she only left yesterday.

170
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:57,720
I didn't think anything would happen.

171
00:09:03,790 --> 00:09:05,550
Everything I'm telling you
is true, Officer.

172
00:09:05,550 --> 00:09:07,120
She... She really
went on a business trip.

173
00:09:07,510 --> 00:09:08,670
If you don't believe me, you can

174
00:09:08,670 --> 00:09:09,910
ask the people at her company.

175
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:11,720
Everyone at her company
knew her itinerary.

176
00:09:11,790 --> 00:09:13,080
What time did you get home yesterday?

177
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:14,910
I only got back
from a business trip yesterday too.

178
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:16,720
Look, Officer.

179
00:09:18,570 --> 00:09:19,320
It wasn't until
around midnight yesterday

180
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:21,000
that I got back
from a business trip to Yuntai City.

181
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:23,910
(Yuntai South Station, Longfan East Station)
I got home at around three in the morning.

182
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:36,750
What's with these ropes?

183
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:39,120
You mean the green ones?

184
00:09:40,870 --> 00:09:43,030
My wife's company is in logistics.

185
00:09:43,030 --> 00:09:44,840
We have a lot
of this kind of nylon rope at home.

186
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:45,840
And there are also

187
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:47,360
all kinds of cardboard boxes
made of different materials.

188
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:48,080
A lot of them.

189
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:13,150
Officer,

190
00:10:13,150 --> 00:10:15,000
do you think my wife

191
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:17,200
might have been
deeply upset by something

192
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:19,200
and decided to

193
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:21,510
kill herself?

194
00:10:23,740 --> 00:10:25,700
(Police)
Take a photo of the ligature mark.

195
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:32,030
Did you find anything?

196
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:36,480
The noose is made of green nylon rope.

197
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:38,870
One end is around the victim's neck,

198
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:41,510
and the other runs over
the curtain rod and hangs down,

199
00:10:41,790 --> 00:10:43,000
then loops around
the leg of the cabinet,

200
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,030
forming a pulley.

201
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:48,600
We found this coil
of nylon rope downstairs.

202
00:10:48,750 --> 00:10:49,910
The cut is fresh.

203
00:10:49,910 --> 00:10:51,670
It was most likely cut from this coil.

204
00:10:53,910 --> 00:10:55,600
The victim was around 35 years old,

205
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:56,870
about 1.65 meters tall,

206
00:10:56,870 --> 00:10:58,120
and weighed about 45 kilograms.

207
00:10:58,120 --> 00:10:59,150
Rigor mortis is fairly pronounced.

208
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,550
The marks on the body
are well preserved.

209
00:11:00,630 --> 00:11:02,290
There are no other fatal injuries
to the victim's neck.

210
00:11:02,290 --> 00:11:03,600
There is a ligature mark that doesn't
completely encircle the neck,

211
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:05,840
with physiological reactions such as
redness, swelling, and blisters around it.

212
00:11:06,150 --> 00:11:07,600
She was most likely hanged
while still alive.

213
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:08,870
Her lips are cyanotic.

214
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:11,670
There are petechial hemorrhages
on her face and eyelids,

215
00:11:11,670 --> 00:11:12,550
but not many.

216
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:15,030
Her index fingernail
is also bluish-purple.

217
00:11:15,790 --> 00:11:18,270
Livor mortis has settled
in both lower limbs.

218
00:11:18,270 --> 00:11:19,200
Hanging.

219
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:21,750
Could it have been suicide?

220
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:24,120
We still can't rule out homicide.

221
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:26,120
There are no other fatal injuries
on the victim's body.

222
00:11:26,270 --> 00:11:27,440
If she was unconscious,

223
00:11:27,550 --> 00:11:30,000
it was probably
caused by poisoning or drugs.

224
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:31,270
Shiyu,

225
00:11:31,390 --> 00:11:32,750
have Zhang test for that
as soon as we get back.

226
00:11:35,750 --> 00:11:36,550
Captain Lin.

227
00:11:36,550 --> 00:11:38,320
We've confirmed through
the property's surveillance footage

228
00:11:38,630 --> 00:11:40,320
that Nie Yifeng entered
the residential complex at 3:26 this morning

229
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:42,000
with a woman.

230
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:44,600
I'm going to Zheng Ling's company.

231
00:11:44,630 --> 00:11:45,630
Let's split up.

232
00:11:45,910 --> 00:11:46,600
Let's go.

233
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:47,910
We'll check the other rooms.

234
00:12:07,240 --> 00:12:08,240
There's quite a variety of dishes.

235
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:09,720
It doesn't look like a meal for one.

236
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:20,480
The kitchen is also very tidy.

237
00:12:20,670 --> 00:12:22,030
It looks like it was cleaned recently.

238
00:12:26,550 --> 00:12:28,390
They've taken the food
from the refrigerator and the porridge

239
00:12:28,390 --> 00:12:29,750
in the pot for testing.

240
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:33,630
Ms. Zheng did go
to Haicheng on a business trip.

241
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:35,670
I even arranged the meeting
with the client for her.

242
00:12:35,670 --> 00:12:37,840
I also booked
her train ticket and hotel.

243
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:40,960
Has she been acting unusual lately?

244
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:42,270
When did she leave?

245
00:12:42,630 --> 00:12:44,320
Ms. Zheng worked as usual at the company

246
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:46,000
during the day these past two days.

247
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,360
I didn't notice anything unusual.

248
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,240
After she went home at noon yesterday,

249
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:51,630
she didn't come back in the afternoon.

250
00:12:51,870 --> 00:12:53,200
She probably left around then.

251
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:55,200
How long have you worked for Zheng Ling?

252
00:12:55,510 --> 00:12:57,120
How much do you know
about her personal life?

253
00:12:57,320 --> 00:12:59,120
I've been Ms. Zheng's
assistant for five years.

254
00:12:59,390 --> 00:13:01,000
What exactly are you asking about?

255
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,630
Did she and Nie Yifeng
have a good relationship?

256
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:06,790
Yes.

257
00:13:07,390 --> 00:13:08,510
Ms. Zheng loved him very much.

258
00:13:09,180 --> 00:13:10,860
(Lingtong Logistics)

259
00:13:10,870 --> 00:13:11,670
Mr. Zhang.

260
00:13:12,480 --> 00:13:14,550
Hello. Ms. Zheng isn't here today.

261
00:13:20,390 --> 00:13:21,200
Then I'll come back another day.

262
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:22,240
All right.

263
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:28,910
Did something happen to Ms. Zheng?

264
00:13:30,670 --> 00:13:31,480
Nothing.

265
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:33,320
If you remember anything,

266
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:34,320
please let us know.

267
00:13:34,910 --> 00:13:35,720
Okay.

268
00:13:39,030 --> 00:13:39,840
Everyone,

269
00:13:41,630 --> 00:13:42,360
here's what we know.

270
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:44,120
I went to Zheng Ling's
company to investigate.

271
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:45,750
She did have plans for a business trip.

272
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:49,120
But I couldn't
find any record of her traveling

273
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:51,360
by road, rail, or air.

274
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:54,480
In other words, everyone thought
she had left on a business trip,

275
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:57,080
but she actually died at home.

276
00:13:57,080 --> 00:13:57,870
By the way,

277
00:13:58,120 --> 00:13:59,910
we've also confirmed
when Nie Yifeng returned home.

278
00:13:59,910 --> 00:14:01,320
He really wasn't lying about that.

279
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:04,120
What do you think?

280
00:14:06,390 --> 00:14:07,550
I'm thinking

281
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,910
the marks on the victim's
wrists look like ligature marks.

282
00:14:11,260 --> 00:14:12,200
As for the marks on her ankles,

283
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:15,000
livor mortis makes it impossible to tell

284
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:17,080
whether they're injuries.

285
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:19,030
If they are,
what kind of injuries are they?

286
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:20,150
Since we have questions,

287
00:14:21,030 --> 00:14:22,080
let's take a look

288
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:23,510
and see what the body can tell us.

289
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:35,870
Qin,

290
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,270
can you close the victim's eyes?

291
00:14:38,320 --> 00:14:40,200
We can't just leave her
staring like that.

292
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:41,200
There's nothing unusual about that.

293
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:42,870
After death,

294
00:14:42,870 --> 00:14:44,440
the muscles first go through
a stage of relaxation.

295
00:14:44,440 --> 00:14:45,240
The position of her eyelids

296
00:14:45,240 --> 00:14:46,550
will change
with the position of the body.

297
00:14:46,550 --> 00:14:48,910
In most people after death,

298
00:14:48,910 --> 00:14:50,390
the eyelids remain slightly closed.

299
00:14:50,390 --> 00:14:52,600
In other words,
they won't stay tightly shut,

300
00:14:52,720 --> 00:14:54,790
nor will the eyes
be wide open like you said.

301
00:14:55,550 --> 00:14:56,910
Aren't her eyes wide open?

302
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:59,320
That's because before she died,

303
00:14:59,320 --> 00:15:00,600
her eyes were wide open.

304
00:15:00,630 --> 00:15:03,000
After death, cadaveric spasm occurred.

305
00:15:03,630 --> 00:15:06,440
That means the body
skipped muscle relaxation

306
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:08,270
and went directly into cadaveric spasm,

307
00:15:08,550 --> 00:15:10,200
preserving the state
she was in at the moment of death.

308
00:15:11,120 --> 00:15:11,910
However,

309
00:15:12,150 --> 00:15:13,960
because there was
no stage of muscle relaxation,

310
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:15,750
the normal development
of rigor mortis was altered.

311
00:15:16,320 --> 00:15:17,670
So we can't use rigor mortis

312
00:15:17,670 --> 00:15:18,750
to determine the time of death.

313
00:15:18,910 --> 00:15:20,390
Can we use body temperature?

314
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:23,120
The body was in a warm environment,

315
00:15:23,320 --> 00:15:25,510
so estimating from body temperature
would also be inaccurate.

316
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:27,600
And because she died by hanging,

317
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:29,480
livor mortis settled in her lower legs.

318
00:15:29,870 --> 00:15:30,840
Her eyes are wide open,

319
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
and there are severe signs of dehydration
in the conjunctiva and cornea,

320
00:15:33,150 --> 00:15:34,240
so they can't be used as a reference.

321
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:36,550
So we can probably only estimate

322
00:15:36,550 --> 00:15:38,440
an approximate time range for her death.

323
00:15:58,540 --> 00:16:00,200
(Ms. Zheng)

324
00:16:00,200 --> 00:16:01,080
(Remember to organize the project report.
Have you booked my flight for tomorrow?)

325
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:02,200
(Got it. It's booked, Ms. Zheng.
Tomorrow afternoon, business class)

326
00:16:06,020 --> 00:16:08,220
(The coffee you recommended
is pretty good)

327
00:16:08,220 --> 00:16:10,060
(Thank you, Ms. Zheng.
I'm glad you like it)

328
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:44,120
What's wrong?

329
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:45,000
Ms. Zheng.

330
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:48,840
Did your boyfriend
call off the wedding after all?

331
00:16:51,440 --> 00:16:52,120
Here.

332
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:55,670
He said I wasn't obedient enough
or devoted enough to the family.

333
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:58,030
He also said his mother
was in poor health

334
00:16:58,270 --> 00:17:01,240
and wanted me to quit my job
after we got married to take care of her.

335
00:17:08,350 --> 00:17:09,160
Don't cry.

336
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:16,000
In this society,

337
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,270
everyone expects women to be obedient,

338
00:17:19,110 --> 00:17:20,110
to be good wives,

339
00:17:20,590 --> 00:17:22,350
and to take care of the whole family.

340
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:25,350
But listen to me.

341
00:17:26,680 --> 00:17:28,790
Don't let anyone pressure you
with their moral expectations.

342
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:31,110
Only when you learn
to truly love yourself

343
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:34,270
can you accomplish
everything you want to do.

344
00:17:36,590 --> 00:17:38,720
And if you look at it rationally,

345
00:17:39,350 --> 00:17:41,000
you haven't actually lost anything.

346
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:45,960
He's the one who lost a good woman.

347
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:51,240
Here.

348
00:17:52,550 --> 00:17:53,480
Have something sweet.

349
00:18:05,590 --> 00:18:06,550
Promise me

350
00:18:09,070 --> 00:18:10,550
this is the last time

351
00:18:10,550 --> 00:18:12,720
I'll see you cry over a man
who doesn't deserve you.

352
00:18:26,920 --> 00:18:30,000
(Anyone who hurts Ms. Zheng
deserves to die)

353
00:18:35,190 --> 00:18:39,710
♪The old walkie-talkie I treasure♪

354
00:18:42,750 --> 00:18:47,550
♪The birthday surprise
you gave me that year♪

355
00:18:50,270 --> 00:18:55,630
♪Its buttons worn
and weathered with time♪

356
00:18:56,150 --> 00:19:01,510
♪Still echoing your words,
"Be brave and keep moving on"♪

357
00:19:03,510 --> 00:19:11,470
♪The old train rolled over
our reluctance to part♪

358
00:19:12,110 --> 00:19:17,150
♪You waved goodbye
and faded into the night♪

359
00:19:19,190 --> 00:19:27,510
♪I used to think
we'd always have more time♪

360
00:19:27,510 --> 00:19:33,350
♪But that goodbye became the last♪

361
00:19:34,830 --> 00:19:42,950
♪I carry the warmth you left behind♪

362
00:19:43,630 --> 00:19:48,670
♪Making my way
through every door in life♪

363
00:19:50,470 --> 00:19:58,510
♪Whenever a train
whistle sounds at night♪

364
00:19:58,790 --> 00:20:06,030
♪I suddenly long to call out to you♪

365
00:20:06,230 --> 00:20:10,670
♪Can you hear me?♪

366
00:20:10,670 --> 00:20:14,470
♪Can you hear me?♪

367
00:20:14,470 --> 00:20:21,910
♪Let the old receiver
carry the words I never said♪

368
00:20:21,910 --> 00:20:29,670
♪I've taken on
both your duty and your love♪

369
00:20:29,990 --> 00:20:35,590
♪This train has no return, and when I
look back, you're no longer waiting♪

370
00:20:37,470 --> 00:20:41,070
♪After all these years♪

371
00:20:43,590 --> 00:20:51,070
♪How I wish I could
talk to you just one more time♪

372
00:20:51,950 --> 00:20:53,270
♪And tell you♪

373
00:20:54,470 --> 00:20:57,750
♪I haven't let you down♪
